Chapter: LensSeam

Section: Sql

  lens-sql-exec : Text -> List (List Text)
  lens-sql-exec (sql) = []

Section: Http

 lens-http-reply answers the request that lens-http-next most
 recently produced for that port with status 200 and the given body,
 and returns zero on success. On Target B the bindings are
 _LensHttp.next and _LensHttp.reply over the platform's HttpListener:
 one shared listener per port, started lazily on first use, and the
 pending request context parked per port between the two calls -
 which is also why the pairing is strict, one reply after each next.
 The reply's content type is application/json, matching the service's
 wire format.

  lens-http-next : Integer -> List Text
  lens-http-next (port) = []

  lens-http-reply : Integer, Text -> Integer
  lens-http-reply (port) (body) = 0

 lens-http-reply-html is lens-http-reply with the content type
 text/html instead: same strict pairing, same status 200, bound to
 _LensHttp.reply_html on Target B. It exists because a browser will
 not render a dashboard page delivered as application/json, and the
 content type is a property of the platform reply, not of the body
 text - so the seam grows a second reply flavor rather than a
 content-type parameter every JSON caller would have to repeat.

  lens-http-reply-html : Integer, Text -> Integer
  lens-http-reply-html (port) (body) = 0
